<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petronas Twin Towers</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1998">1998</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petronas">Petronas</a> Twin Towers are a pair of 88-storey skyscrapers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuala-lumpur">Kuala Lumpur</a>, Malaysia, designed by César Pelli and completed in 1998. At 452 metres they were the tallest buildings in the world until 2004 and remain the tallest twin towers. Joined by a skybridge, they house the headquarters of Petronas and became symbols of Malaysia's economic ambitions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/petronas-twin-towers.jpg" alt="Petronas Twin Towers" width="320" height="182" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petronas_Towers_Logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
